Bug patch cheval26-small-subgroup, ported to libsignal v0.105.4 (b2a5c30f3245c1bcad04b27b1e752a38321c793d).

Derived from Signal Messenger's libsignal (https://github.com/signalapp/libsignal):
Copyright 2020-2026 Signal Messenger, LLC. SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
(full text: ../../../LICENSE). See ../../README.md.

Reverses upstream commit 5293caa6cad81566b80f3c3731857bedaa78737b ("protocol: Check that base
keys are torsion free and in range"; the exact upstream diff is
upstream-5293caa6cad81566b80f3c3731857bedaa78737b.diff next to this file) on the v0.105.4 tree.
The upstream diff does not reverse-apply there: commit 5cf8b0d71 ("Refactor 1:1 messaging code")
moved Bob's key agreement, and with it the base-key check, from `initialize_bob_session`
(rust/protocol/src/ratchet.rs) into `pqxdh_accept` (rust/protocol/src/pqxdh.rs). Hunk by hunk:
  * rust/core/src/curve.rs, rust/protocol/Cargo.toml: the upstream hunks, reversed (they
    reverse-apply by three-way merge);
  * rust/protocol/src/pqxdh.rs: the moved `is_canonical` check removed (upstream's ratchet.rs
    hunk), and the two imports only it used;
  * rust/protocol/tests/ratchet.rs: upstream's two added tests removed;
  * Cargo.lock: upstream's added `curve25519-dalek` dependency line removed.
git apply ignores this preamble.

